# Shared run_log

All Crazyflie scripts must use `run_log.py` for console output and CSV/telemetry logs. Do not use bare `print()`, ad-hoc loggers, or homemade CSV writers.

Read and follow `.agents/skills/run-log/SKILL.md` (also `.cursor/skills/run-log` and `.claude/skills/run-log`).

## Required

```python
import run_log
log = run_log.setup(__file__)
```

- `log.info` / `log.warning` / `log.error` instead of `print`
- CSVs via `run_log.csv_path(...)` + `run_log.write_csv(...)` (script + timestamp metadata)
- Extend `run_log.py` if you need new logging features — do not invent a parallel module

Reference: `flip.py`, `script.py`.
